---
layout: layouts/base.njk
bodyClass: "location"
---
{#
  Layout for the location pages — /ai-training-<location>/.

  Reuses the .ind class family from the industry pages on purpose: they are the
  same kind of page doing the same job from the other direction, and a second
  near-identical stylesheet would only be a second thing to keep in sync.

  The cross-reference is the point of these pages. Each one names the industries
  that actually cluster in that area and links to their page; each industry page
  names all seven areas. Neither has to win "AI training Australia" for the pair
  to answer "AI training for NDIS providers in Logan".

  Honesty rule enforced by the `presence` field: only the Gold Coast (head
  office) and Adelaide (sales office) are places Ad On Group actually sits. Every
  other page says plainly that it is a service area reached from the Gold Coast.
  Implying seven offices would be a lie a prospect can check in one search.

  Front matter each page supplies:
    title, description, permalink, location, region, h1, eyebrow, lede,
    presence, contextHeading, context: [str], industriesHere: [{url, why}],
    deliveryNote, faq: [{q, a}], closer
#}
<main class="ind">

  <section>
    <p class="ind-eyebrow">{{ eyebrow or ("AI training in " ~ location) }}</p>
    <h1>{{ h1 }}</h1>
    <p class="ind-lede">{{ lede | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/programs/">See the program</a>
    </div>
    <p class="ind-trust">
      Ad On Group has been Australian-owned since 2008 and is rated 4.8 from 229 Google
      reviews. Our AI training is delivered by Claude Certified Associates, and 40+
      Australian businesses have completed the program.
    </p>
  </section>

  {% if context and context.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>{{ contextHeading or ("Why " ~ location + " businesses are asking") }}</h2>
    {% for c in context %}<p>{{ c | safe }}</p>{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# The cross-reference. Each industry named here links to its own page, and
     that page names this location back. #}
  {% if industriesHere and industriesHere.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>The sectors we see most in {{ location }}</h2>
    <p>
      The program is the same three months wherever you are. What changes is the examples
      and the workflows, which follow the work your team actually does.
    </p>
    <div class="ind-grid">
      {% for ih in industriesHere %}
        {% for i in industries.items %}{% if i.url == ih.url %}
        <article class="ind-card">
          <h3><a href="{{ i.url }}">{{ i.label }}</a></h3>
          <p>{{ ih.why | safe }}</p>
        </article>
        {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="ind-note">
      <h2>How the training reaches {{ location }}</h2>
      <p>{{ presence | safe }}</p>
      {% if deliveryNote %}<p>{{ deliveryNote | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
      <p>
        The program itself runs online and self-paced — 24 modules over three months, around
        two hours a week — so nobody loses a day travelling to a classroom. What we teach is
        tool-agnostic, and <a href="/ongoing-support/">ongoing support</a> comes with every
        program: monthly webinars, tool masterclasses, a support hour and an active community.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ai-quiz/">Take the free AI audit</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if faq and faq.length %}
  <section>
    <h2>Questions {{ location }} teams ask</h2>
    {% for item in faq %}
    <details>
      <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
      <div><p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p></div>
    </details>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <h2>We also train teams in</h2>
    <div class="ind-more">
      {% for l in locations.items %}{% if l.slug != slug %}
        {% if l.hasPage %}<a href="/ai-training-{{ l.slug }}/">{{ l.name }}</a>
        {% else %}<span class="ind-place">{{ l.name }}</span>{% endif %}
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>{{ closerHeading or ("Get your " ~ location + " team started") }}</h2>
    <p>{{ closer | safe }}</p>
    <div class="ind-actions">
      <a class="ind-cta" href="/ai-enquiry/">Book a time to talk</a>
      <a class="ind-cta-alt" href="/ad-on-ai-division/">About Ad On AI</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
